1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
[Netero] Wait.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Exchanging words?

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Hey, King…

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
would you like to know your name?

5
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
I bet I'm the only one who knows now.

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Those same subordinates probably died
fighting your Royal Guard.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
[wind blowing]

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
I'll make you a deal.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
If you can force me to admit defeat,

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
I'll tell you your name.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,000
[King] Force you?

12
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
But without killing you?

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
[scoffs]

14
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,000
[tense music playing]

15
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
So I'll be playing
without a rook and bishop.

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
[opening theme music playing]

17
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

18
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
[singer singing in English]

19
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

20
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,000
[singer singing in English]

21
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

22
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
CENTIPEDE X AND X MEMORY

23
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
[narrator] As the King and Netero prepared

24
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
for what they were both certain
would be their final battle…

25
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
[dramatic music playing]

26
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:28,000
[narrator] Ikalgo continued to cry
deep beneath the palace,

27
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
[Ikalgo sobbing]

28
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
[remote beeps]

29
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
[Ikalgo continues sobbing]

30
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
I have to do this.

31
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
I have to!

32
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
[gags]

33
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
This is no time for tears.

34
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
I have to find Palm.

35
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
[gasps]

36
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
The door to the warehouse area is open.

37
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
[Welfin] I've got a lot
of questions I wanna ask you,

38
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
but if you try anything funny,

39
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
you're dead.

40
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[Ikalgo] I've got a pretty good idea
about what he wants to know…

41
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,000
And he'll use any means necessary
to find out.

42
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:37,000
If I start leaking information,
people could die.

43
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
But if he's a Manipulator,

44
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,000
he can obtain the information
against my will.

45
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Huh? Stop right there.

46
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
I really will kill you!

47
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[Ikalgo] Kill me, then.
That's what I want.

48
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Stop now!

49
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[Ikalgo] I won't betray my friends,

50
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
but I'll take you with me!

51
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
[screams]

52
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
[Welfin] Now you've done it, you bastard!

53
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Missileman!

54
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
[whimpers]

55
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
[groans]

56
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
[Ikalgo] Hey, I'm not dead.

57
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
I didn't sustain any damage.

58
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
What was that attack?

59
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
[Welfin] Ah, damn it.

60
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
That really hurts.

61
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Why, you little punk.

62
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
You'll pay for this.

63
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
That bastard.

64
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
I'll take my time beating him to a pulp.

65
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[chuckles]

66
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
[Ikalgo] Wait. He planted
something living inside me?

67
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
-[crunch]
-[groans]

68
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:29,000
They grow by feeding
on your defiance, so get ready.

69
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
[groaning]

70
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
If you disobey my orders

71
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Huh?

72
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Hey, what are you doing, idiot?

73
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Didn't you listen to a word I just said?

74
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
If you try what I think
you're going to try…

75
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
[gasping]

76
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
All that's fine by me.

77
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
And if I die, so be it.

78
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
[inhales]

79
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Ahh! No!

80
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
No, stop!

81
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
[Ikalgo groaning]

82
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
[Welfin] Wait a minute.

83
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
If he wanted to kill me,

84
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
that's the ultimate form of resistance.

85
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Now it'll take no time at all

86
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
for the black centipedes to grow
large enough to kill him.

87
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
I just need to make sure you stay put.

88
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
I still have ammunition.

89
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[tense music playing]

90
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Don't mess with me, bastard!

91
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
You are so dead.

92
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
I'll kill you, you hear me!

93
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
-[inhales]
-[Welfin screaming]

94
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
[groaning]

95
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[centipedes clattering]

96
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,000
[Ikalgo laughing]

97
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,000
[Welfin] Huh?

98
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,000
[tense music playing]

99
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
[centipedes rustling]

100
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
[dramatic music playing]

101
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[imperceptible]

102
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
I get it, okay?

103
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Look, I won't go anywhere! I promise!

104
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
I give up, so, please, don't shoot.

105
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
[Ikalgo] The pain is going away.

106
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:56,000
The creatures inside me are in agony?

107
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
[Welfin] Damn it. You win.

108
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,000
I saw it coming.

109
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,000
I just had a feeling
this would happen eventually.

110
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
who didn't have any regard
for their own life.

111
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
so do you think you could
get rid of all these bugs now?

112
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
[Welfin groans] Shut the hell up.

113
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
I'm in too much pain
to think about that right now.

114
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Hmm?

115
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:51,000
[groans]

116
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Uh…

117
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Hurry up, will you?

118
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
[Welfin] Just give me a minute.

119
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Damn, I don't have a way
to deactivate Missileman.

120
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:07,000
But if I tell him the truth,
I'm in real trouble.

121
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
How am I gonna get out of this?

122
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
[tense music playing]

123
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
I need to buy some time.

124
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
-[centipedes rustling]
-[Ikalgo growls]

125
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
[Ikalgo] Then hurry up,
and get rid of these things.

126
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Welfin chuckles nervously]

127
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Well, I, um…

128
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
[Ikalgo] Hmm?

129
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
[groans]

130
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Oh, well. Forget it.

131
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
No, wait! Hold on a minute!

132
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:14,000
I can't remove them now,
not once they've been activated.

133
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Sorry, but it's true.

134
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:29,000
[Ikalgo] The insects are in pain again.

135
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Thing is, I only attack to kill someone,

136
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
and screw what happens next.

137
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:45,000
I never gave a single thought
to what happened to my enemy afterwards.

138
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Huh?

139
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
[Ikalgo] I once knew someone
just like him.

140
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
I'm curious.

141
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
[groans]

142
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[dramatic music playing]

143
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
[Welfin] Fine. You win.

144
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,000
When I woke up, my first thought was…

145
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
[sighs]

146
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
Damn it.

147
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
I still remember it like it was yesterday.

148
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
[automatic guns firing]

149
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:21,000
[Welfin] Those monster bugs
killed me in the NGL.

150
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:38,000
And soon, I was reborn as something new.

151
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Even now, I can still remember
the one thing that…

152
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
that I most wanted to forget…

153
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
The sight of my father strangling me,

154
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:01,000
and the woman behind him just watching.

155
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:09,000
In the beginning,
I only had little flashbacks of it,

156
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,000
but over time, I remembered
everything that happened.

157
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
My little brother saved me…

158
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,000
even though we weren't related by blood.

159
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,000
He looked just like…

160
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Gyro does!

161
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
[gasps] Gyro?

162
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
You know him as the King.

163
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
We used to fight
about whose life was worse.

164
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
When I had to laugh to keep from crying,

165
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
he was always there.

166
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
We were both empty,

167
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:59,000
and I guess, looking back,

168
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,000
that's why we had nothing to hide.

169
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
[sighs]

170
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Sometimes I wonder what he's doing.

171
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Oh. Those weaklings wanted
the treasure in the back,

172
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
so I let them in.

173
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Don't worry. They're not a threat.

174
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,000
I was watching you and Blo on the monitor,

175
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
[Ikalgo gags]

176
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
[Ikalgo sobbing]

177
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
[Ikalgo] I'm a coward!

178
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
[sobbing]

179
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,000
[Welfin] That's all.

180
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Once I saw that you couldn't finish Blo,

181
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:01,000
I figured you'd be an easy target,

182
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,000
but now I see I was wrong.

183
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
[sighs]

184
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
You go ahead.

185
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
I'm way too tired.

186
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,000
[Ikalgo] One last question.

187
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Did you see a woman in the palace?

188
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
A woman?

189
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
They called it Number One.

190
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
[sighs]

191
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Thanks a lot!

192
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,000
Hmm.

193
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
[narrator] Welfin had spent his life

194
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:10,000
unable to trust himself or others.

195
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Telling Ikalgo the location
of the woman he was searching for

196
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:18,000
was the first time he had
ever opened up to someone,

197
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
spoken from the heart, and told the truth.

198
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[cracking]

199
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
[fluid sloshing]

200
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
[closing theme music playing]

201
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
[Gon] What's wrong, Killua?
